                  "id": "KzfdN",
                  "name": "Note",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1000,
                  "content": "Directions are double-encoded — tint and icon (config in the 'Direction → Icon config' frame). That stays. What changes is that the tints get harmonised and each one gains a paired ink, so the colour carries information instead of decoration: today every chip prints #18181B on a tint of a random lightness, and three warm tints, three greens and two pinks are indistinguishable at chip size.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "iSOUE",
              "name": "Option A — harmonised 18",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "#FAFAF9",
              "cornerRadius": 12,
              "stroke": "#0000000F",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "strokeAlignment": "inner",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 12,
              "padding": 20,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "uKGa6",
                  "name": "Head",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 3,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "fNA2i",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "#18181B",
                      "content": "OPTION A · one tint per direction, harmonised",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "700",
                      "letterSpacing": 0.8
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "eSqyW",
                      "name": "D",
                      "fill": "#74746F",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Same 18 hues, pulled to a common lightness (L≈93) but keeping real chroma — a chip has to read as coloured, not grey. Ink is the tint's own hue at L≈25, which ties the icon to its chip while staying crisp: the pairs measure 7.2–9.2:1, where a mid-dark ink measured ~6:1 and washed out at 16px. Bottom strip shows today's value for comparison.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
