                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "by3PM",
                  "name": "Note",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1000,
                  "content": "You are right that a wall of red buttons would collide with error states. So the brand colour never becomes a button surface inside the product: it becomes the colour of orientation — where you are, what is selected, what is focused. The button that commits stays graphite. Filled red is reserved for the one destructive confirmation.",
